---
import BaseLayout from '@/components/layout/BaseLayout.astro';
import Icon from '@/components/ui/Icon.astro';
import Logo from '@/components/ui/Logo.astro';
import MondayContactForm from '@/components/forms/MondayContactForm.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Register Your Site - REDI Sites"
  description="Register your commercial property for a REDI readiness evaluation by the Site Selectors Guild."
  noindex
>
  <section class="bg-steel-100 pt-32 pb-24">
    <div class="container-page">
      <div
        class="bg-steel-200/70 shadow-lifted relative mx-auto max-w-[900px] rounded-3xl px-6 py-8 sm:px-12 sm:py-10"
      >
        <a
          href="/"
          class="text-ink-600 hover:text-ink-900 absolute top-6 right-6 transition-colors sm:top-8 sm:right-8"
          aria-label="Close and return home"
        >
          <Icon name="x" size={22} />
        </a>
        <Logo variant="nav" class="mx-auto" />

        <a
          href="/sign-in"
          class="font-heading text-ink-700 hover:text-ink-900 mt-8 inline-flex items-center gap-1 text-sm font-bold tracking-wide uppercase transition-colors"
        >
          <Icon name="chevron-left" size={16} />
          Back
        </a>
        <h1 class="mt-1 text-4xl sm:text-[2.75rem]">Sign Up</h1>
        <p class="text-ink-600 mt-1 text-lg">Access REDI SITES tools &amp; value.</p>

        <div class="shadow-soft mt-8 rounded-2xl bg-white p-6 sm:p-10">
          <h2 class="font-heading text-navy-950 text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl">
            Begin Your Site's Readiness Journey
          </h2>
          <p class="text-ink-600 mt-4 leading-relaxed">
            REDI Sites is the first national site readiness designation program in the United
            States, developed in affiliation with the Site Selectors Guild — the only association of
            the world's foremost professional site selection consultants.
          </p>
          <p class="text-ink-600 mt-4 leading-relaxed">
            Every site that completes the process earns a designation reflecting its current level
            of readiness: Emerging, Bronze, Silver, Gold or Platinum. There's no pass or fail.
            You'll come away with a clear, independent picture of where your site stands today and
            exactly what it takes to reach the next level.
          </p>

          <p class="font-heading text-ink-800 mt-6 text-sm font-bold tracking-wide uppercase">
            Here's How It Works
          </p>
          <ol class="mt-3 space-y-3">
            <li class="text-ink-600 flex gap-3 leading-relaxed">
              <span
                class="bg-navy-950 font-heading mt-0.5 flex size-6 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full text-xs font-bold text-white"
              >
                1
              </span>
              <span>
                <strong class="text-ink-800">Register your site</strong> using this form, it takes about
                two minutes. The registration fee is $450 per site.
              </span>
            </li>
            <li class="text-ink-600 flex gap-3 leading-relaxed">
              <span
                class="bg-navy-950 font-heading mt-0.5 flex size-6 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full text-xs font-bold text-white"
              >
                2
              </span>
              <span
                ><strong class="text-ink-800">Pay securely</strong> through QuickBooks or by check.</span
              >
            </li>
            <li class="text-ink-600 flex gap-3 leading-relaxed">
              <span
                class="bg-navy-950 font-heading mt-0.5 flex size-6 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full text-xs font-bold text-white"
              >
                3
              </span>
              <span>
                <strong class="text-ink-800">Get access to Lasso</strong>, where your team completes
                the site's RFI and uploads supporting documentation.
              </span>
            </li>
          </ol>

          <p class="text-ink-600 mt-6 leading-relaxed">
            From there, your submission is evaluated by Terracon, an independent engineering firm,
            and reviewed by a committee of Site Selectors Guild members — the same consultants who
            advise companies on where to invest.
          </p>
          <p class="text-ink-600 mt-4 leading-relaxed">
            Before you begin, please confirm your site meets the three program minimums: located in
            the United States, at least 5 acres and available for sale or lease.
          </p>
          <p class="text-ink-600 mt-4 leading-relaxed">
            Registering multiple sites or a portfolio? Email{' '}
            <a
              href="mailto:Nicki@REDISites.com"
              class="text-navy-700 font-semibold underline underline-offset-2 transition-colors hover:text-cyan-600"
            >
              Nicki@REDISites.com
            </a>{' '}
            and we'll set everything up for you.
          </p>

          <a
            href="#register-form"
            class="font-heading text-navy-950 shadow-soft hover:shadow-card mt-8 flex h-[48px] w-full items-center justify-center rounded-lg bg-cyan-400 text-sm font-semibold tracking-wide uppercase transition-all duration-200 hover:bg-cyan-300 sm:w-auto sm:px-8"
          >
            Register My Site
          </a>
        </div>

        <div id="register-form" class="mt-10 scroll-mt-10">
          <MondayContactForm formId="474841603e14828e7b565d097a98ad89" />
        </div>

        <!--
          TODO(auth): this form is a Monday.com lead-intake embed, not a
          real account-creation flow - there is still no self-serve account
          registration anywhere in this build. If/when that's built, this is
          where it goes. Nothing to reuse from SetPasswordForm.tsx besides
          the general form/validation pattern.
            1. Expected request:  POST /api/auth/register
               { email, password, name, company?, ...whatever fields the
               client wants collected - none are specified yet, this needs
               product input, not just engineering }.
            2. Role assignment: decide what WordPress user role a self-
               registered account gets by default (e.g. a restricted
               "member" role, not "subscriber"/"administrator") - must be
               enforced server-side; nothing here should let a client-
               supplied field set its own role.
            3. Expected response (success): 201 + either an auto-login
               session (see sign-in.astro TODO) or an "check your email to
               verify" flow - decide before building, this changes the UX
               significantly.
            4. Expected response (failure): 409 for "email already
               registered" (again, consider enumeration implications - see
               forgot-password.astro TODO), 422 for validation errors with
               field-level error detail.
            5. Add the same password-strength validation used in
               SetPasswordForm.tsx (`setPasswordSchema`, currently defined
               only in that file - consider extracting it to a shared
               `src/lib/validation/` module, which exists but is currently
               empty, once more than one form needs the same rules).
        -->
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
